<http://smart.who.int/base/CodeSystem/KGL2DMNClasses> a fhir:CodeSystem ;
  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:Resource.id [ fhir:value "KGL2DMNClasses"] ;
  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "generated" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><div xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\"><hr/><p><b>English</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: CodeSystem KGL2DMNClasses</b></p><a name=\"KGL2DMNClasses\"> </a><a name=\"hcKGL2DMNClasses\"> </a><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://smart.who.int/base/CodeSystem/KGL2DMNClasses</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">dmn-definitions<a name=\"KGL2DMNClasses-dmn-definitions\"> </a></td><td>DMN File</td><td>One DMN file as a unit -- the `dmn:definitions` root. Shares its IRI with the l1:external-artifact for the same file, so the l2:decision-support-logic component that points at it and this subgraph name one resource.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">dmn-decision<a name=\"KGL2DMNClasses-dmn-decision\"> </a></td><td>DMN Decision</td><td>A `dmn:decision` -- the question being answered, and the node that carries the link back to the BPMN task invoking it. A file may hold several; the BCG file holds one.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">dmn-decision-table<a name=\"KGL2DMNClasses-dmn-decision-table\"> </a></td><td>DMN Decision Table</td><td>The table realising a decision. Separate from dmn-decision because DMN permits other expression kinds -- a literal expression, an invocation -- and collapsing the two would make the graph unable to say which was used.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">dmn-input-clause<a name=\"KGL2DMNClasses-dmn-input-clause\"> </a></td><td>DMN Input Clause</td><td>An input column. Its expression text is where data element names are embedded, which is the only reason this is a node rather than a property of the table.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">dmn-output-clause<a name=\"KGL2DMNClasses-dmn-output-clause\"> </a></td><td>DMN Output Clause</td><td>An output column. The BCG table's four are Care Plan, Guidance displayed to health worker, Annotations and Reference(s). These are column DEFINITIONS in a decision table, not clinical records: no edge from this class reaches an execution artefact, and none may.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">dmn-rule<a name=\"KGL2DMNClasses-dmn-rule\"> </a></td><td>DMN Rule</td><td>One row. Its input and output cells are carried as properties, not nodes: 250 of them in the BCG table alone, none the target of a cross-model edge. What the rule needs a node for is its citation edge into L1.</td></tr></table></div><div xml:lang=\"fr\" lang=\"fr\"><hr/><p><b>French</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Narratif généré : CodeSystem KGL2DMNClasses</b></p><a name=\"fr-KGL2DMNClasses\"> </a><a name=\"fr-hcKGL2DMNClasses\"> </a><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://smart.who.int/base/CodeSystem/KGL2DMNClasses</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Affichage</b></td><td><b>Définition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">dmn-definitions<a name=\"fr-KGL2DMNClasses-dmn-definitions\"> </a></td><td>DMN File</td><td>One DMN file as a unit -- the `dmn:definitions` root. Shares its IRI with the l1:external-artifact for the same file, so the l2:decision-support-logic component that points at it and this subgraph name one resource.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">dmn-decision<a name=\"fr-KGL2DMNClasses-dmn-decision\"> </a></td><td>DMN Decision</td><td>A `dmn:decision` -- the question being answered, and the node that carries the link back to the BPMN task invoking it. A file may hold several; the BCG file holds one.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">dmn-decision-table<a name=\"fr-KGL2DMNClasses-dmn-decision-table\"> </a></td><td>DMN Decision Table</td><td>The table realising a decision. Separate from dmn-decision because DMN permits other expression